      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronson%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name was shortened to Bronson in 1871 when the Lake Shore & Michigan Southern Railroad built a station here.",
